IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P3-section-3`

-- P3-art-18: Article 18 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): documentation keeping.
-- Lines 412-421 of the consolidated text. Unchanged by the Omnibus. Article 2(13) names Article 18 among the obligations whose application may be limited for an Article 6(1) system (the gate).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE met / the period runs; JUST FALSE the duty applies and is not met, or the stated period is over (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a));
-- NOTHING not covered (the group does not yet apply, Art 2(13) may limit the Article, the paragraph limits itself, or the text points to a Member State's law outside the sources).

§ `Article 18(1): keeping the documentation at the disposal of the national competent authorities for a period ending 10 years after placing on the market`

-- "for a period ending 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service": the last day of the period is the tenth anniversary of the placement
-- (a whole number of years added by `add years`; an anniversary that does not exist is clamped to the last day of the month). The text gives no start: the period is read as running from the placement (fork F-18-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:414 | 1. The provider shall, for a period ending 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service, keep at the disposal of the national competent authorities:
@ref Art 18(1) (src:414)
GIVEN `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 18(1) the last day of the period for keeping the documentation` MEANS
    `add years` (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`) 10

-- Is the date asked within the period? JUST FALSE once the period has ended (a period fixed in the text's own words); NOTHING before the placement (the text is silent on a start).
-- src:414 | 1. The provider shall, for a period ending 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service, keep at the disposal of the national competent authorities:
@ref Art 18(1) (src:414)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 18(1) the period for keeping the documentation runs on the date asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF (Day `the date asked`) LESS THAN (Day (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names the end of the period, not its start
        ELSE IF (Day `the date asked`) AT MOST (Day (`Art 18(1) the last day of the period for keeping the documentation` `the AI system`))
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period ending 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service" (the period has ended)
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 18, "", 0)

§ `Article 18(1)(a) to (e): the five kinds of documents`

-- src:415 | (a) the technical documentation referred to in Article 11;
-- src:416 | (b) the documentation concerning the quality management system referred to in Article 17;
-- src:417 | (c) the documentation concerning the changes approved by notified bodies, where applicable;
-- src:418 | (d) the decisions and other documents issued by the notified bodies, where applicable;
-- src:419 | (e) the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47.
@ref Art 18(1)(a) to (e) (src:415-419)
DECLARE `Art 18(1) what is kept at the disposal of the national competent authorities` HAS
    `the technical documentation referred to in Article 11`                                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- (a)
    `the documentation concerning the quality management system referred to in Article 17`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b)
    `there are changes approved by notified bodies`                                              IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c) "where applicable"
    `the documentation concerning the changes approved by notified bodies`                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c)
    `there are decisions or other documents issued by notified bodies`                          IS A BOOLEAN  -- (d) "where applicable"
    `the decisions and other documents issued by the notified bodies`                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- (d)
    `the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47`                                IS A BOOLEAN  -- (e)

-- Points (c) and (d) say "where applicable": a document that does not exist because there is no approved change or no decision is not required.
-- src:415 | (a) the technical documentation referred to in Article 11;
-- src:416 | (b) the documentation concerning the quality management system referred to in Article 17;
-- src:417 | (c) the documentation concerning the changes approved by notified bodies, where applicable;
-- src:418 | (d) the decisions and other documents issued by the notified bodies, where applicable;
-- src:419 | (e) the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47.
@ref Art 18(1)(a) to (e) (src:415-419)
GIVEN `the documents` IS AN `Art 18(1) what is kept at the disposal of the national competent authorities`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 18(1) the documents listed in points (a) to (e) are kept` MEANS
        `the documents`'s `the technical documentation referred to in Article 11`
    AND `the documents`'s `the documentation concerning the quality management system referred to in Article 17`
    AND ((NOT `the documents`'s `there are changes approved by notified bodies`) OR `the documents`'s `the documentation concerning the changes approved by notified bodies`)
    AND ((NOT `the documents`'s `there are decisions or other documents issued by notified bodies`) OR `the documents`'s `the decisions and other documents issued by the notified bodies`)
    AND `the documents`'s `the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47`

-- src:414 | 1. The provider shall, for a period ending 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service, keep at the disposal of the national competent authorities:
@ref Art 18(1) (src:414)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the documents` IS AN `Art 18(1) what is kept at the disposal of the national competent authorities`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 18(1) the provider keeps the documents at the disposal of the national competent authorities` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `Art 18(1) the period for keeping the documentation runs on the date asked` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN
            IF `Art 18(1) the documents listed in points (a) to (e) are kept` `the documents`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provider shall, for a period ending 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service, keep at the disposal of the national competent authorities: (a) ... (e)"
        ELSE IF `Art 18(1) the period for keeping the documentation runs on the date asked` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` EQUALS JUST FALSE
             THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period ending 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service" (the period has ended: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a); fork F-18-1)
             ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names the end of the period, not its start (the date asked is before the placement; fork F-18-1)
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 18, "", 0)

§ `Article 18(2): the Member State determines conditions for a provider or its representative that goes bankrupt or ceases its activity`

-- The paragraph addresses the Member State (an official, so no seat): it matters to the provider because it says that the documentation stays at the authorities' disposal when the provider
-- or its authorised representative established on the Member State's territory goes bankrupt or ceases its activity before the end of the period. The conditions are the Member State's, outside the sources.
-- JUST TRUE: the paragraph applies to these facts and the Member State is to determine the conditions; NOTHING: the paragraph does not speak to them (silent).
-- src:420 | 2. Each Member State shall determine conditions under which the documentation referred to in paragraph 1 remains at the disposal of the national competent authorities for the period indicated in that paragraph for the cases when a provider or its authorised representative established on its territory goes bankrupt or ceases its activity prior to the end of that period.
@ref Art 18(2) (src:420)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the provider or its authorised representative is established on the territory of the Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider or its authorised representative goes bankrupt or ceases its activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the provider or its authorised representative went bankrupt or ceased its activity` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 18(2) the Member State is to determine the conditions under which the documentation remains at the disposal of the national competent authorities` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF       `the provider or its authorised representative is established on the territory of the Member State`
             AND `the provider or its authorised representative goes bankrupt or ceases its activity`
             AND (Day `the date the provider or its authorised representative went bankrupt or ceased its activity`) AT MOST (Day (`Art 18(1) the last day of the period for keeping the documentation` `the AI system`))
        THEN JUST TRUE  -- the conditions themselves are the Member State's: outside the sources
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph 2 speaks only of a provider or authorised representative established on the Member State's territory that goes bankrupt or ceases its activity prior to the end of the period
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 18, "", 0)

§ `Article 18(3): financial institutions maintain the technical documentation as part of the documentation they keep under financial services law`

-- src:421 | 3. Providers that are financial institutions subject to requirements regarding their internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law shall maintain the technical documentation as part of the documentation kept under the relevant Union financial services law.
@ref Art 18(3) (src:421)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the provider is a financial institution subject to requirements regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation is maintained as part of the documentation kept under the relevant Union financial services law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 18(3) the provider that is a financial institution has maintained the technical documentation as part of the documentation kept under financial services law` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the provider is a financial institution subject to requirements regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Providers that are financial institutions subject to requirements regarding their internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law shall maintain" (the provider is not such an institution)
        ELSE
             IF `the technical documentation is maintained as part of the documentation kept under the relevant Union financial services law`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Providers that are financial institutions subject to requirements regarding their internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law shall maintain the technical documentation as part of the documentation kept under the relevant Union financial services law"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 18, "", 0)

@ref Art 18(3) (src:421)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the provider is a financial institution subject to requirements regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 18 act`
`Art 18(3) the provider's duty to maintain the technical documentation as part of the documentation kept under financial services law` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the provider is a financial institution subject to requirements regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law`
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 18(3) maintain the technical documentation as part of the documentation kept under the relevant Union financial services law`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the technical documentation was not maintained as part of the documentation kept under the relevant Union financial services law"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the provider is not a financial institution of that kind
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 18, "", 0)


§ `Regulative rules of Article 18 (paragraph 1 as a prohibition derived from the duty to keep; paragraph 2 on the Member State)`

DECLARE `Art 18 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 18(1) cease to keep at the disposal of the national competent authorities the documentation listed in points (a) to (e)`
    `Art 18(3) maintain the technical documentation as part of the documentation kept under the relevant Union financial services law`

-- "shall ... keep at the disposal ... for a period ending 10 years after": the duty to keep, with its stated period, is written as a prohibition on ceasing to keep during the period
-- (the SHANT derived from the flat "shall", ruling N2 of 2026-11-04). The clock is in days from the date asked (day 0); the window closes on the last day of the period.
-- An act on a day after the window closes is no violation. Nothing is owed when the gate is shut or the date asked is already past the period.
-- src:414 | 1. The provider shall, for a period ending 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service, keep at the disposal of the national competent authorities:
@ref Art 18(1) (src:414)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 18 act`
`Art 18(1) the provider's duty to keep the documentation at the disposal of the national competent authorities for the period` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Provider
         SHANT `Art 18(1) cease to keep at the disposal of the national competent authorities the documentation listed in points (a) to (e)`
         WITHIN daysLeft
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the documentation was no longer kept at the disposal of the national competent authorities before the end of the period ending 10 years after the high-risk AI system was placed on the market or put into service"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 18, "", 0)
        lastDay MEANS `Art 18(1) the last day of the period for keeping the documentation` `the AI system`
        daysLeft MEANS IF (Day lastDay) AT LEAST (Day `the date asked`) THEN (Day lastDay) MINUS (Day `the date asked`) ELSE 0

DECLARE `Art 18(2) body` IS ONE OF
    `Art 18(2) Member State`

DECLARE `Art 18(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 18(2) determine the conditions under which the documentation remains at the disposal of the national competent authorities`

-- The Member State "shall determine conditions": no time limit and no consequence the text states, so no trace can show a breach.
-- src:420 | 2. Each Member State shall determine conditions under which the documentation referred to in paragraph 1 remains at the disposal of the national competent authorities for the period indicated in that paragraph for the cases when a provider or its authorised representative established on its territory goes bankrupt or ceases its activity prior to the end of that period.
@ref Art 18(2) (src:420)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 18(2) body` `Art 18(2) act`
`Art 18(2) the Member State's duty to determine the conditions` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY `Art 18(2) Member State`
         MUST `Art 18(2) determine the conditions under which the documentation remains at the disposal of the national competent authorities`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 18(2) Member State` BECAUSE "the Member State did not determine the conditions under which the documentation remains at the disposal of the national competent authorities"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 18, "", 0)
